{"step_index":113,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:22:20Z","input_tokens":6347,"cache_read_tokens":237859,"output_tokens":9129,"thinking":"The observed workflow suggests a processing pipeline: environment, animation, sound effects, verification, and coordination. This sequence implies a data flow from initial environment setup to final coordinated output. Planning to execute a verification script and subsequently develop a comprehensive verification suite.\n\n\nVerification script execution aims to cover all V6 deliverables in a single run, triggered by calls to the verifier function. Detailed criteria are defined, including byte-for-byte SHA256 audits for V5 files to ensure isolation, referencing a baseline hash file. Additionally, headless Blender audits are planned for specific V6 blend files.\n\n\nThe scene utilizes non-photorealistic rendering with a comic book aesthetic, indicated by the absence of raytracing and specific node group configurations. There's a dynamic `sv_dimension` variable that changes across different acts, influencing visual elements. Primary car components feature 3D ink outlines achieved through modifiers and backface culling.\n\nAdditional graphic speed effects are present, along with smooth camera movements and a consistent frame rate of 12 fps, ensuring no judder, even on chase-cam shots.\n\n\nThe animation is confirmed at 24 fps with linear interpolation, contrasting with the car's secondary motion, which employs a stepped constant interpolation at two frames. Motion blur shutter setting is approximately 0.07.\n\nA multi-pass compositor node setup, named \"Comp\\_V6\\_SpiderVerse,\" uses enabled view layer passes for varied effects. This includes Kuwahara filtering, edge ink filtering, CMYK misregistration simulation, paper grain, speed lines, and specific duotone frames along with portal glitch spikes. Evaluating CPU render speed with a test frame.\n\n\nFocusing on image verification. Checking for the existence and integrity of specified PNG and JPG files within the texture, stills, and clips directories. Assessing image quality, particularly luminance, saturation, and contrast in the still images, paying attention to color palettes and identifying potential graphic impact frames.\n\n\nAnalyzing audio and video files. Verified sound effects WAV file for energy spikes at designated portal glitch and impact frames using audio analysis tools. Checked M4A file for volume levels and confirmed MP4 video files had valid streams, frame rates, and audio parameters, noting no clipping.\n\nExamining documentation to confirm comprehensive explanation of the Spider-Verse architecture, color script, animation techniques, compositor setup, stylized SFX, and reproduction instructions. Confirming that all V5 links remain intact while adding the V6 section in the readme files.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python \"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\\snapshot_v5_hashes.py\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Snapshot V5 baseline SHA256 hashes"}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"\nRead-only V6 Spider-Verse Headless Blender Verification Suite\nChecks v6_stage_lookdev.blend and v6_stage_anim_sv.blend:\n- EEVEE raytracing=False, motion_blur_shutter (~0.07)\n- sv_dimension 3-Act evaluation (Act I=0.0, Act II=1.0, Act III=2.0)\n- NG_SV_ComicSurface (ShaderToRGB, Window coords, Rim LayerWeight)\n- 3D Inverted-Hull Ink Outlines (Solidify + MAT_SV_InkOutline backface culling)\n- V6_09_ComicFX collection (aero vortex ribbons + wheel smear arcs, 0 camera obstructions)\n- Safe On-Twos: Bone_Root/Bone_Heading/Cameras stay 24fps LINEAR; secondary motion stepped on Twos (CONSTANT)\n- Multi-pass Compositor (ViewLayer passes + Kuwahara + Filter + CMYK Separate/Translate/Combine)\n- 1080p CPU single-frame render speed benchmark (to scratch/ ONLY)\n\"\"\"\nimport bpy\nimport os\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom mathutils import Vector\n\nPROJ = r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\"\nSCRATCH = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\"\nLOOKDEV_BLEND = os.path.join(PROJ, \"v6_spiderverse\", \"v6_stage_lookdev.blend\")\nANIM_SV_BLEND = os.path.join(PROJ, \"v6_spiderverse\", \"v6_stage_anim_sv.blend\")\nOUT_JSON = os.path.join(SCRATCH, \"v6_blender_report.json\")\n\ndef iter_fcurves(action):\n    fcs = list(getattr(action, \"fcurves\", []) or [])\n    if fcs:\n        return fcs\n    for layer in getattr(action, \"layers\", []) or []:\n        for strip in getattr(layer, \"strips\", []) or []:\n            for cb in getattr(strip, \"channelbags\", []) or []:\n                fcs.extend(cb.fcurves)\n    return fcs\n\nreport = {}\n\n# 1. Check lookdev blend exists & basic stats\nif os.path.exists(LOOKDEV_BLEND):\n    bpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=LOOKDEV_BLEND)\n    sc_ld = bpy.context.scene\n    report[\"lookdev_blend\"] = {\n        \"exists\": True,\n        \"total_objects\": len(bpy.data.objects),\n        \"use_raytracing\": sc_ld.eevee.use_raytracing,\n        \"has_sv_dimension\": \"sv_dimension\" in sc_ld,\n        \"has_NG_SV_ComicSurface\": \"NG_SV_ComicSurface\" in bpy.data.node_groups,\n        \"has_V6_09_ComicFX\": \"V6_09_ComicFX\" in bpy.data.collections,\n    }\nelse:\n    report[\"lookdev_blend\"] = {\"exists\": False}\n\n# 2. Deep audit of v6_stage_anim_sv.blend\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=ANIM_SV_BLEND)\nscene = bpy.context.scene\nrig = bpy.data.objects[\"RIG_F1_Race\"]\n\n# 2a. Render & ViewLayer settings\nvl = scene.view_layers[0]\nvl_passes = {\n    \"use_pass_normal\": getattr(vl, \"use_pass_normal\", False),\n    \"use_pass_mist\": getattr(vl, \"use_pass_mist\", False),\n    \"use_pass_z\": getattr(vl, \"use_pass_z\", False),\n    \"use_pass_emit\": getattr(vl, \"use_pass_emit\", False),\n    \"use_pass_cryptomatte_object\": getattr(vl, \"use_pass_cryptomatte_object\", False),\n}\n\n# 2b. NPR Shader NodeGroup & Outline check\nng_comic = bpy.data.node_groups.get(\"NG_SV_ComicSurface\")\nng_comic_node_types = sorted({n.type for n in ng_comic.nodes}) if ng_comic else []\n\nink_mat = bpy.data.materials.get(\"MAT_SV_InkOutline\")\nink_info = None\nif ink_mat:\n    ink_info = {\n        \"use_backface_culling\": getattr(ink_mat, \"use_backface_culling\", None),\n        \"use_backface_culling_shadow\": getattr(ink_mat, \"use_backface_culling_shadow\", None),\n    }\nsolidify_objs = []\nfor o in bpy.data.objects:\n    for m in o.modifiers:\n        if m.type == 'SOLIDIFY' and m.use_flip_normals:\n            solidify_objs.append(o.name)\n\n# 2c. V6_09_ComicFX check\nfx_coll = bpy.data.collections.get(\"V6_09_ComicFX\")\nfx_objs = [{\"name\": o.name, \"parent\": o.parent.name if o.parent else None, \"parent_bone\": o.parent_bone} for o in fx_coll.all_objects] if fx_coll else []\n\n# 2d. 3-Act sv_dimension evaluation\nsv_dim_samples = {}\nfor label, f in ((\"Act1_f100\", 100), (\"Act2_f1200\", 1200), (\"Act3_f1800\", 1800)):\n    scene.frame_set(f)\n    dg = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n    sc_e = scene.evaluated_get(dg)\n    sv_dim_samples[label] = round(float(sc_e.get(\"sv_dimension\", -999.0)), 3)\n\n# 2e. Safe On-Twos (12fps) vs Smooth 24fps World/Cam check\nrig_fc_interp = {}\nif rig.animation_data and rig.animation_data.action:\n    for fc in iter_fcurves(rig.animation_data.action):\n        interps = sorted({kp.interpolation for kp in fc.keyframe_points})\n        # Check step spacing on CONSTANT fcurves\n        xs = [kp.co.x for kp in fc.keyframe_points[:10]]\n        avg_dx = round((xs[-1] - xs[0]) / max(1, len(xs) - 1), 2) if len(xs) > 1 else 0\n        rig_fc_interp[f\"{fc.data_path}[{fc.array_index}]\"] = {\"interps\": interps, \"sample_dx\": avg_dx, \"n_keys\": len(fc.keyframe_points)}\n\ncam_non_linear = []\nfor o in bpy.data.objects:\n    if o.type == 'CAMERA' and o.name.startswith(\"Cam_S\"):\n        if o.animation_data and o.animation_data.action:\n            for fc in iter_fcurves(o.animation_data.action):\n                if any(kp.interpolation == 'CONSTANT' for kp in fc.keyframe_points):\n                    cam_non_linear.append(f\"{o.name}:{fc.data_path}\")\n\n# 2f. Compositor Node Tree inspection\ncomp_ng = getattr(scene, \"compositing_node_group\", None) or getattr(scene, \"node_tree\", None)\ncomp_nodes = []\nif comp_ng:\n    def collect_nodes(nt, prefix=\"\"):\n        for n in nt.nodes:\n            comp_nodes.append(f\"{prefix}{n.type}:{n.name}\")\n            if n.type == 'GROUP' and getattr(n, \"node_tree\", None):\n                collect_nodes(n.node_tree, prefix=f\"{n.name}/\")\n    collect_nodes(comp_ng)\n\n# 2g. 26-Shot Camera LOS check (verify V6_09_ComicFX / outlines never block cameras!)\nmarkers = sorted(scene.timeline_markers, key=lambda m: m.frame)\nshots_windows = []\nfor i, mk in enumerate(markers):\n    f0 = mk.frame\n    f1 = (markers[i + 1].frame - 1) if (i + 1 < len(markers)) else scene.frame_end\n    shots_windows.append((mk.name, f0, f1, mk.camera))\n\ncar_and_fx = {o.name for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'MESH' and not o.name.startswith(\"V5_\")}\nfx_names = {o[\"name\"] for o in fx_objs}\nocc_hits = []\nonboard_fx_hits = []\nfor s_name, f0, f1, cam in shots_windows:\n    is_onboard = \"Onboard\" in s_name\n    for f in range(f0, f1 + 1, 8):\n        scene.frame_set(f)\n        dg = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\n        cam_e = cam.evaluated_get(dg)\n        rig_e = rig.evaluated_get(dg)\n        cp = cam_e.matrix_world.translation.copy()\n        if not is_onboard:\n            rp = (rig_e.matrix_world @ rig_e.pose.bones[\"Bone_Root\"].matrix).translation + Vector((0, 0, 0.5))\n            dv = rp - cp\n            hit, loc, _, _, ho, _ = scene.ray_cast(dg, cp + dv.normalized() * 0.05, dv.normalized(), distance=dv.length - 0.15)\n            if hit and ho and ho.name not in car_and_fx:\n                occ_hits.append({\"shot\": s_name, \"f\": f, \"blocker\": ho.name})\n        else:\n            cam_fwd = (cam_e.matrix_world.to_3x3() @ Vector((0, 0, -1))).normalized()\n            hit, loc, _, _, ho, _ = scene.ray_cast(dg, cp + cam_fwd * 0.1, cam_fwd, distance=3.0)\n            if hit and ho and ho.name in fx_names:\n                onboard_fx_hits.append({\"shot\": s_name, \"f\": f, \"fx_blocker\": ho.name, \"dist\": round((loc - cp).length, 2)})\n\n# 2h. 1080p CPU Render Speed Benchmark (warm frame to scratch/)\nscene.render.resolution_x = 1920\nscene.render.resolution_y = 1080\nscene.render.resolution_percentage = 100\nbench_sec = {}\nfor bf in (100, 1320):\n    for s_name, f0, f1, cam in shots_windows:\n        if f0 <= bf <= f1:\n            scene.camera = cam\n            break\n    scene.frame_set(bf)\n    scene.render.filepath = os.path.join(SCRATCH, f\"v6_bench_{bf:04d}.jpg\")\n    t0 = time.perf_counter()\n    bpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)\n    bench_sec[str(bf)] = round(time.perf_counter() - t0, 3)\n\nreport[\"anim_sv_blend\"] = {\n    \"total_objects\": len(bpy.data.objects),\n    \"root_objects\": [o.name for o in scene.collection.objects],\n    \"use_raytracing\": scene.eevee.use_raytracing,\n    \"motion_blur_shutter\": round(scene.render.motion_blur_shutter, 4),\n    \"view_layer_passes\": vl_passes,\n    \"ng_comic_node_types\": ng_comic_node_types,\n    \"ink_outline_mat\": ink_info,\n    \"solidify_outline_obj_count\": len(solidify_objs),\n    \"solidify_sample\": solidify_objs[:12],\n    \"comic_fx_count\": len(fx_objs),\n    \"comic_fx_objs\": fx_objs,\n    \"sv_dimension_3acts\": sv_dim_samples,\n    \"rig_fcurves\": rig_fc_interp,\n    \"cam_constant_violations\": cam_non_linear,\n    \"scene_use_nodes\": scene.use_nodes,\n    \"compositor_node_count\": len(comp_nodes),\n    \"compositor_nodes\": comp_nodes,\n    \"occ_hits\": occ_hits,\n    \"onboard_fx_hits\": onboard_fx_hits,\n    \"bench_1080p_sec\": bench_sec,\n}\n\nwith open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(report, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(\"V6_BLENDER_REPORT_WRITTEN:\", OUT_JSON)\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\\verify_v6_blender.py"}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"\nRead-only V6 Spider-Verse Isolation, Stills, Poster, Clips, Audio & Docs Verification\nStrictly uses PIL/NumPy + ffprobe/ffmpeg + wave/numpy + SHA256 (NEVER LLM binary read_file!).\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport glob\nimport json\nimport wave\nimport hashlib\nimport subprocess\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nPROJ = r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\"\nSCRATCH = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\"\nV5_HASH_JSON = os.path.join(SCRATCH, \"v5_baseline_hashes.json\")\nFFMPEG = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\scoop\\shims\\ffmpeg.exe\"\nFFPROBE = r\"C:\\Users\\86052\\scoop\\shims\\ffprobe.exe\"\nOUT_TXT = os.path.join(SCRATCH, \"v6_media_docs_report.txt\")\n\nlines = []\n\n# 1. Verify 100% V5 Isolation via SHA256 baseline + LATEST directory listing\nlines.append(\"=== 1. V5 ISOLATION SHA256 CHECK ===\")\nbase = json.load(open(V5_HASH_JSON, encoding=\"utf-8\"))\nv5_diffs = []\nfor rel, meta in base.items():\n    fp = os.path.join(PROJ, rel)\n    if not os.path.exists(fp):\n        v5_diffs.append(f\"DELETED: {rel}\")\n        continue\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(fp, \"rb\") as f:\n        while True:\n            b = f.read(1024 * 1024)\n            if not b:\n                break\n            h.update(b)\n    if h.hexdigest() != meta[\"sha256\"]:\n        v5_diffs.append(f\"MODIFIED: {rel}\")\nlatest_files = sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(PROJ, \"LATEST\")))\nlines.append(f\"  Checked {len(base)} V5 files -> diffs={len(v5_diffs)} ({v5_diffs})\")\nlines.append(f\"  LATEST/ contents: {latest_files}\")\nlines.append(\"\")\n\n# 2. Check V6 Textures\nlines.append(\"=== 2. V6 SPIDER-VERSE TEXTURES ===\")\nv6_tex_dir = os.path.join(PROJ, \"v6_spiderverse\", \"textures\")\nif os.path.exists(v6_tex_dir):\n    for fn in sorted(os.listdir(v6_tex_dir)):\n        fp = os.path.join(v6_tex_dir, fn)\n        if os.path.isfile(fp) and fn.lower().endswith((\".png\", \".jpg\")):\n            im = Image.open(fp).convert(\"RGB\")\n            arr = np.asarray(im, dtype=np.float32)\n            lines.append(f\"  {fn:<26} size={im.size} bytes={os.path.getsize(fp):>8} meanRGB={[round(float(x),1) for x in arr.mean(axis=(0,1))]}\")\nelse:\n    lines.append(\"  MISSING v6_spiderverse/textures!\")\nlines.append(\"\")\n\n# 3. Check V6 Stills + contact_sheet_v6.jpg + comic_page_sheet.jpg\nlines.append(\"=== 3. V6 STILLS & COMIC PAGE POSTER ===\")\nstills_dir = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v6\", \"stills\")\nif os.path.exists(stills_dir):\n    sfiles = sorted(f for f in os.listdir(stills_dir) if f.lower().endswith((\".jpg\", \".png\")))\n    lines.append(f\"  Total files in renders_v6/stills: {len(sfiles)}\")\n    lines.append(f\"  {'File':<34} {'SizePx':<14} {'Bytes':>9} {'MeanL':>6} {'P05':>5} {'P95':>5} {'SatMean':>7} {'Clip%':>6}\")\n    for fn in sfiles:\n        fp = os.path.join(stills_dir, fn)\n        im = Image.open(fp).convert(\"RGB\")\n        arr = np.asarray(im, dtype=np.float32)\n        lum = 0.2126 * arr[:, :, 0] + 0.7152 * arr[:, :, 1] + 0.0722 * arr[:, :, 2]\n        mx = arr.max(axis=2)\n        mn = arr.min(axis=2)\n        sat = np.where(mx > 1.0, (mx - mn) / np.maximum(mx, 1.0), 0.0)\n        p05, p95 = [float(x) for x in np.percentile(lum, [5, 95])]\n        clip_pct = float((mx >= 250).mean() * 100.0)\n        lines.append(f\"  {fn:<34} {str(im.size):<14} {os.path.getsize(fp):>9} {lum.mean():>6.1f} {p05:>5.1f} {p95:>5.1f} {sat.mean():>7.3f} {clip_pct:>6.2f}\")\nelse:\n    lines.append(\"  MISSING renders_v6/stills!\")\nlines.append(\"\")\n\n# 4. Check 3x 96-frame Showcase Clip Sequences + Impact Frame signature (f=1698..1699)\nlines.append(\"=== 4. V6 3x 96-FRAME CLIP SEQUENCES & IMPACT FRAME CHECK ===\")\nCLIPS = [\n    (\"clip1_miles_1610\", 61, 156),\n    (\"clip2_gwen_65\", 1290, 1385),\n    (\"clip3_2099_impact\", 1650, 1745),\n]\nfor cname, f0, f1 in CLIPS:\n    cdir = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v6\", \"clips_frames\", cname)\n    if not os.path.exists(cdir):\n        lines.append(f\"  {cname}: MISSING DIR!\")\n        continue\n    present = [f for f in range(f0, f1 + 1) if os.path.exists(os.path.join(cdir, f\"f_{f:04d}.jpg\"))]\n    im0 = Image.open(os.path.join(cdir, f\"f_{present[0]:04d}.jpg\")) if present else None\n    # Check frame-to-frame difference on sample consecutive frames (confirm smooth 24fps camera vs frozen frames)\n    diffs = []\n    for ff in range(f0, min(f0 + 8, f1)):\n        p_a = os.path.join(cdir, f\"f_{ff:04d}.jpg\")\n        p_b = os.path.join(cdir, f\"f_{ff+1:04d}.jpg\")\n        if os.path.exists(p_a) and os.path.exists(p_b):\n            aa = np.asarray(Image.open(p_a).convert(\"RGB\"), dtype=np.float32)\n            bb = np.asarray(Image.open(p_b).convert(\"RGB\"), dtype=np.float32)\n            diffs.append(round(float(np.abs(aa - bb).mean()), 2))\n    lines.append(f\"  {cname:<22} expected={f1-f0+1} found={len(present)} res={im0.size if im0 else None} step_MAD_first8={diffs}\")\n\n# Check Impact Frame f=1698..1699 vs f=1695 in clip3_2099_impact\nc3dir = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v6\", \"clips_frames\", \"clip3_2099_impact\")\nfor ff in (1695, 1697, 1698, 1699, 1700, 1701):\n    fp = os.path.join(c3dir, f\"f_{ff:04d}.jpg\")\n    if os.path.exists(fp):\n        arr = np.asarray(Image.open(fp).convert(\"RGB\"), dtype=np.float32)\n        lum = 0.2126 * arr[:, :, 0] + 0.7152 * arr[:, :, 1] + 0.0722 * arr[:, :, 2]\n        bw_extreme = float(((lum < 25.0) | (lum > 220.0)).mean() * 100.0)\n        lines.append(f\"    ImpactCheck f={ff}: meanL={lum.mean():.1f} stdL={lum.std():.1f} extremeBW%={bw_extreme:.1f}% meanRGB={[round(float(x),1) for x in arr.mean(axis=(0,1))]}\")\nlines.append(\"\")\n\n# 5. Check V6 WAV + M4A + 4 MP4s\nlines.append(\"=== 5. V6 AUDIO & MP4 DELIVERABLES ===\")\nwav_sv = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v6\", \"sfx_spiderverse_90s.wav\")\nif os.path.exists(wav_sv):\n    with wave.open(wav_sv, \"rb\") as wf:\n        ch, sw, sr, nf = wf.getnchannels(), wf.getsampwidth(), wf.getframerate(), wf.getnframes()\n        pcm = np.frombuffer(wf.readframes(nf), dtype=np.int16).reshape(-1, ch).astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n    peak_db = 20.0 * np.log10(max(float(np.abs(pcm).max()), 1e-9))\n    clipped = int((np.abs(pcm) >= 0.999).sum())\n    # Check RMS around portal cuts & impact frame (70.71s)\n    def win_rms_db(t_sec, w=0.18):\n        i0 = max(0, int((t_sec - w/2) * sr))\n        i1 = min(nf, int((t_sec + w/2) * sr))\n        return round(20.0 * np.log10(max(float(np.sqrt(np.mean(pcm[i0:i1] ** 2))), 1e-9)), 2)\n    lines.append(f\"  sfx_spiderverse_90s.wav: {sr}Hz {sw*8}bit {ch}ch dur={nf/sr:.4f}s peak={peak_db:.2f}dBFS clipped={clipped}\")\n    lines.append(f\"    Portal1(32.8s)={win_rms_db(32.8)}dB | Portal2(66.7s)={win_rms_db(66.7)}dB | ImpactStowe(70.71s)={win_rms_db(70.71)}dB (vs pre-impact 70.2s={win_rms_db(70.2)}dB)\")\nelse:\n    lines.append(\"  MISSING sfx_spiderverse_90s.wav!\")\n\nV6_MEDIA = [\n    \"sfx_spiderverse_90s.wav\",\n    \"audio_v6_sv_mix_90s.m4a\",\n    \"clip1_miles_1610.mp4\",\n    \"clip2_gwen_65.mp4\",\n    \"clip3_2099_impact.mp4\",\n    \"v6_spiderverse_showcase_12s.mp4\",\n]\nfor fn in V6_MEDIA:\n    fp = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v6\", fn)\n    if not os.path.exists(fp):\n        lines.append(f\"  {fn}: MISSING!\")\n        continue\n    pr = subprocess.run([FFPROBE, \"-v\", \"error\", \"-show_format\", \"-show_streams\", \"-of\", \"json\", fp],\n                        capture_output=True, text=True, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    info = json.loads(pr.stdout) if pr.stdout else {}\n    fmt = info.get(\"format\", {})\n    s_desc = []\n    for st in info.get(\"streams\", []):\n        if st.get(\"codec_type\") == \"video\":\n            s_desc.append(f\"V:{st.get('codec_name')} {st.get('width')}x{st.get('height')} r={st.get('r_frame_rate')} nb={st.get('nb_frames')}\")\n        elif st.get(\"codec_type\") == \"audio\":\n            s_desc.append(f\"A:{st.get('codec_name')} {st.get('sample_rate')}Hz {st.get('channels')}ch dur={float(st.get('duration', 0)):.3f}s\")\n    vr = subprocess.run([FFMPEG, \"-hide_banner\", \"-i\", fp, \"-vn\", \"-af\", \"volumedetect\", \"-f\", \"null\", \"NUL\"],\n                        capture_output=True, text=True, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    mv = xv = \"?\"\n    for ln in vr.stderr.splitlines():\n        if \"mean_volume:\" in ln: mv = ln.split(\"mean_volume:\")[1].strip()\n        if \"max_volume:\" in ln: xv = ln.split(\"max_volume:\")[1].strip()\n    lines.append(f\"  {fn:<34} size={int(fmt.get('size',0)):>9} dur={float(fmt.get('duration',0)):.4f}s | {' + '.join(s_desc)} | mean={mv}, max={xv}\")\nlines.append(\"\")\n\n# 6. Docs check\nlines.append(\"=== 6. V6 DOCS CHECK ===\")\nfor rel in (\"README.md\", \"docs/README_V6_SPIDERVERSE.md\", \"docs/README_V5.md\"):\n    fp = os.path.join(PROJ, rel)\n    lines.append(f\"  {rel:<30} exists={os.path.exists(fp)} size={os.path.getsize(fp) if os.path.exists(fp) else 0}\")\n\nout_s = \"\\n\".join(lines)\nwith open(OUT_TXT, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(out_s)\nprint(out_s)\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\\verify_v6_media_docs.py"}}]}
